The assessment is at session_plan/assessment.md (7.1 KB). It isn't committed because session_plan/ is gitignored: the plain git add was refused, and I unstaged it after a git add -f slipped it in. The working tree is clean.

The main finding: this assessment run was stopped partway through with [Agent stopped: Max tokens reached (1061497/1000000)]. That is exactly what Yuanhao filed as #999, a 1M-token limit on each request, so I'm treating the issue as a real, live problem. In the code, src/agent_builder.rs:1412-1416 sets the 1M limit explicitly and calls it "a generous default". It's the same as yoagent's default, and it also quietly brings in a 10-minute time limit per request (max_duration 600s in yoagent 0.24.2). The count includes the whole conversation re-sent on every turn, so it runs out around turn 16. I searched the last 4 evolve run logs for the stop message and found nothing. That doesn't prove it never happened there, because yoyo may hide that message when its output goes to a pipe. This run is the one confirmed case.

Other points in the assessment:
• **Recent work:** the symlink escapes for `--allow-dir` are now blocked, after the first attempt was lost to an "Overloaded" error (#996). The rule for dangling symlink entries is decided and covered by tests (#998). build.rs now picks up new commits (#995). yoagent is on 0.24.2.
• **Evolve runs:** none failed. The 19:59 run was cancelled, and the 13:09 run finished with 0 of 1 tasks done.
• **Self-test:** --version shows the current commit (6dba4be0), so #995 works locally. -p printed exactly PONG\n and exited 0.
• **Research:** in the Claude Agent SDK, both `max_turns` and `max_budget_usd` default to "No limit". The budget is set in dollars, and each limit ends with its own stop reason that callers can check. I didn't use yopedia this time, because the run was already over its token budget.
• **Recommendation:** do #999 first. It sits in `agent_builder.rs`, which also follows the trajectory's warning to keep the next diff out of `prompt`. Limits for sub-agents can't change until yoagent#238 is released. For the second slot: #997 (opt-in retry after a partial answer) or one slice of #982 (shell subcommands that report failure but exit 0).
